# state/ — nice-to-have follow-ups

[#211 follow-up] normalize_path_for_write (paths.py) is applied only to
control_root/task_cwd/execution_cwd at spawn/session write sites. Other
persisted path-like fields (claude_config_dir, agent_path, skill_paths) still
accept raw strings — extend the same write-boundary normalization if their
consumers ever compare or dedupe on path equality.

[current-chat settings] Each newly observed conversation stores an immutable
LaunchPolicySnapshot inline in sessions.jsonl, including skill bodies, profile,
env and inventory prompt. This keeps replay independent of a pruned observing
run and preserves the selected chat's policy across /resume -> /new. Measure
journal growth and fold cost before frequent-switch workloads; if material,
deduplicate immutable snapshots by content, without making a cache authoritative
or reverting to the observing run's potentially different settings.
